t></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKABE NORIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAMURA SEIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKABE, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAMURA, SEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A behavior model/action model which serves as a base when a behavior and action of a robot device is produced is changed to another of higher growth level stepwise at a predetermined timing according to the history of inputs from external and the history of the behaviors and actions of the robot device. Thus, a pet robot having a further improved amusability is provided by combining growth and learning.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon la présente invention, on a la possibilité de modifier le modèle initial de comportement ou d'action d'un robot pour en obtenir de nouveaux représentant des étapes progressives de la croissance du robot, selon un calendrier reflétant l'historique des entrées de l'extérieur et l'historique des comportements et des actions du robot. Cela permet de conférer à un robot animal familier un intérêt ludique renouvelé combinant la croissance et l'apprentissage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at